// Time complexity — interview ke liye important
// map internally usually a balanced binary search tree (Red-Black Tree) use karta hai.
// Operation	Time complexity
// Insert/emplace()	\(O(\log n)\)
// Find/count()	\(O(\log n)\)
// erase(key)	\(O(\log n)\)
// Access/update using m[key]	\(O(\log n)\)
// Traversal	\(O(n)\)
//map vs unordered_map vs multimap

// map
// - Keys sorted order mein.
// - Duplicate keys allowed nahi.
// - Operations generally \(O(\log n)\).
// unordered_map
// - Keys ka sorted order nahi hota.
// - Duplicate keys allowed nahi.
// - Operations average \(O(1)\), worst case \(O(n)\).
// multimap
// - Keys sorted order mein.
// - Duplicate keys allowed.
// - Operations generally \(O(\log n)\).
// - m[key] se access nahi kar sakte; iterator ya find() use karo.

